From d4fd2042ecd5f1bbe86749dab6b62aed6b5d2ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:27:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Store proofs in Cloudflare R2 and build the proofing journey
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Proof artwork now lives in an R2 bucket. The bucket is private: nothing is
served from a public URL, every read goes through a signed link that expires,
and the object key is random so one proof can't be guessed from another. Until
the credentials are added, files are written to .uploads/ instead, which a
production build refuses unless ALLOW_LOCAL_UPLOADS is set deliberately — that
flag is how the end-to-end suite walks the journey against a real build.

Around that:

- The studio queue groups work by who it is waiting on, and the dashboard
  counts what is outstanding alongside a turnaround line and designer workload.
- A designer uploads; every upload is a new version and nothing is overwritten.
  Only a proofreader or an admin can send one on or return it with notes.
- The customer sees the artwork itself — a PDF is rendered in the browser
  rather than converted on the server — and clicks it to pin a comment where
  the problem is. Requesting changes needs at least one mark, so the studio
  always knows where to look.
- The staff order page keeps showing the customer's marks after a new version
  is uploaded, since that is exactly when the designer needs them.
- A notification bell in the account sidebar, and a customer dashboard that
  leads with the proof waiting on them rather than a placeholder.

pdf.js 6 calls Map.prototype.getOrInsertComputed, which only reached browsers
during 2025, so it is polyfilled when missing — a good share of the people
approving a funeral proof are on older devices.

Two things the tests turned up on the way: the unit glob only ever matched one
directory deep, so 37 of the 41 unit tests were never running; and the e2e
suite left the database in a state that failed its own second run, so it now
reseeds before every run.

